  "summary": "I added a \"Pause flythrough\" button below the canvas. Clicking it stops the camera in place while the scene keeps rendering. The label then becomes \"Resume flythrough\", and clicking again continues from the same spot. Typecheck passes and the render shows no errors. I only checked the button's initial state in the render and did not click it, so the pause and resume behaviour itself is untested.\n\n`window.__TASK_STATE__` is now `{ flying, cameraX, cameraY, cameraZ }` and is updated every frame. I removed the earlier `time`, `z` and `loopSeconds` fields from it. The button is in `index.html` and the logic is in `src/main.ts`. The camera clock only advances while flying, so the small up-and-down bob also freezes on pause."
